\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3 & =0+0+0+K \\\\ K & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{5}+6{t}^{2}+t-3.\n$$" 13194139534469 true] [17592186289962 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289963 13194139534469 true] [17592186289962 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534469 true] [17592186289962 1041 "field-1" 13194139534469 true] [17592186289962 1104 #edb/ref 17592186289963 13194139534469 true] [17592186289962 1110 #uuid "a588a670-231e-5605-95a4-a382ffcf11db" 13194139534469 true] [17592186289963 1034 "6t^2+t-3" 13194139534469 true] [17592186289963 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534469 true] [17592186289963 1111 #uuid "5c85da6b-693e-5b55-8b2b-cb592647c4b1" 13194139534469 true] [17592186289964 1017 #edb/ref 17592186289965 13194139534469 true] [17592186289964 1089 "q-6255" 13194139534469 true] [17592186289964 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534469 true] [17592186289964 1100 "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with velocity $v(t)=4{t}^{3}+{t}^{2}+6t,$ where $t$ is the time. If the particle is at the position $x=11$ when $t=1,$ calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t>0.$" 13194139534469 true] [17592186289964 1113 #uuid "47fb04f1-6892-5e82-9539-204f7e5c883c" 13194139534469 true] [17592186289964 1145 "We start by integrating the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,dt \\\\  & =\\int (4{t}^{3}+{t}^{2}+6t)dt \\\\  & ={t}^{4}+\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+3{t}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C,$ we use the fact that $x(1)=11.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}11 & =(1)^{4}+\\frac{(1)^{3}}{3}+3(1)^{2}+C \\\\ 11 & =1+\\frac{1}{3}+3+C \\\\ C & =\\frac{20}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{4}+\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+3{t}^{2}+\\frac{20}{3}.\n$$" 13194139534469 true] [17592186289965 1000 #edb/ref 17592186289966 13194139534469 true] [17592186289965 1000 #edb/ref 